2
00:00:31,000 --> 00:00:37,300
I'd like to start by reading a short section of a manuscript I've been working on for about a year now.

3
00:00:37,300 --> 00:00:42,860
And it's talking about this whole seasons of formation that we've been walking through.

4
00:00:42,860 --> 00:00:44,500
And it's titled The Next Season.

5
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:53,720
You do know that human nature is to assume that the state you are in will be perpetual.

6
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:59,480
That if I'm just like bummed, it's never going to be better.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:03,240
Or if I'm doing well, I've got to figure it out now.

8
00:01:03,240 --> 00:01:06,440
And the reality is that there's usually a next season.

9
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:09,940
Today there's a lot of talk about resilience.

10
00:01:09,940 --> 00:01:23,000
Quote, psychologists define resilience as the process of adapting well in the face of adversity, trauma, tragedy, threats, or significant sources of stress.

11
00:01:23,000 --> 00:01:32,900
Seasons of formation are passive ways that God builds resilience into his children.

12
00:01:32,900 --> 00:01:46,720
Just as humans, they naturally need emotional times of stress and repair, activity and rest, intensity and relaxation to build healthy resilience, so too, in our spiritual development.

13
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:53,880
God trains us in holiness, using various seasons at varying times.

14
00:01:53,880 --> 00:02:02,480
Typically, believers begin their journey in a season of delight and enter some of their most challenging times as they mature.

15
00:02:02,480 --> 00:02:08,360
But it would be a mistake to view the seasons as we've presented them as linear.

16
00:02:08,360 --> 00:02:15,140
God does not necessarily lead his children through seasons in the order that we've delivered them.

17
00:02:16,000 --> 00:02:16,740
He is sovereign.

18
00:02:16,740 --> 00:02:21,920
Nor should every season necessarily be viewed as God's scent.

19
00:02:21,920 --> 00:02:30,240
Times of great physical, financial, or relational difficulty that thrust us into a hard life.

20
00:02:30,240 --> 00:02:38,040
Now, God may, in those adverse times, choose to show or hide his presence.

21
00:02:40,240 --> 00:02:42,540
And in doing so, change the season.

22
00:02:42,540 --> 00:02:50,020
But he's not likely the author of your sickness or your financial hardship or your strained relationships.

23
00:02:50,020 --> 00:03:01,420
Those things may be the result of your activity, someone else's activity, or totally unconnected to any particular activity.

24
00:03:02,780 --> 00:03:06,460
Regardless, in the theology of seasons, it doesn't matter.

25
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:17,540
God's promise is to use whatever season you are in, whatever season you are in, regardless of why you are there, to make you more like Jesus.

26
00:03:17,540 --> 00:03:23,040
However you arrived in the desert, did God allure you there?

27
00:03:23,040 --> 00:03:25,700
Did you blindly wander in?

28
00:03:26,300 --> 00:03:29,260
Did it just descend violently upon you?

29
00:03:29,260 --> 00:03:31,880
Avoid the why question.

30
00:03:31,880 --> 00:03:37,740
Instead, remember to focus on the how and the what.

31
00:03:38,280 --> 00:03:43,920
The important formational questions that will help fill your well with living water.

32
00:03:43,920 --> 00:03:49,280
